I've compiled both Nethack and Slash'Em on my Macbook Pro, using BSD-
ish config settings.  The games run fine for the most part, but
garbage symbols appear on the screen sometimes, seemingly most often
when animation is involved (running, zapping a wand that generates a
ray, etc).  Here are some examples:

Doing "liquid leap" on the first turn of my Slash'Em game as a
doppelganger:

 ---.---
 |..@.../5.
 |..d/5.
 |..<..-
 -------

Running down a corridor:

   |.
    .   |50
    # |50
    #50
    #
   `#:0
 ---@--
 |....|
 |....|

"5," "0," and "`" seem to be the most numerous garbage symbols.
Sometimes the "@" character representing me gets left behind when I
run, with the cursor in some different location, so I usually have to
redraw the screen after each time I run, which I do frequently.  Not
fun.

Is there a workaround for this issue?  I see the same behavior when
using the Terminal app, Emacs's terminal emulator, and xterm, so I
suspect it's a problem with OS X's native termcap library.  I could
try downloading and compiling the library myself, I suppose, but is
there some more convenient solution?


